 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.register` and `ToolRegistry.execute` now validate tool inputs against each tool's declared JSON Schema `inputSchema` using `ajv` (`strict: false`, `validateFormats: false`, with no coercion, defaults, or injected `additionalProperties: false`), returning a `ToolResponse` describing failing field paths and expected types on invalid input so the orchestrator feeds rejections back to the model as a `tool_result` without invoking the executor.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Migration:** An executor that previously hand-validated its `input` now receives only arguments that already satisfy its declared `inputSchema` (`required`, property types, and `enum`), and a tool that relied on seeing malformed input inside its executor to produce a custom error message will no longer be called when the schema rejects the input. Undeclared extra properties still pass through unless the tool's `inputSchema` sets `additionalProperties: false`.
+
